<p>Once the inventory is verified, the focus shifts to the functional integrity of the assets. All electrical and mechanical items require immediate testing upon uncrating. Technicians must perform basic operational checks, including power-up sequences, safety mechanism validations, and visual inspections for transit-related damage such as loose components or fluid leaks.</p>
<p>Items that fail these initial tests must be segregated and flagged for technical review, while those that pass are prepared for their next stage of deployment or storage. This proactive testing prevents the discovery of latent defects after installation, thereby saving significant time and resources in the long run.</p>
<p>Concurrently, the placement of clean furniture and sensitive equipment must follow a strict spatial planning strategy. These items are to be positioned in climate-controlled zones or designated staging areas immediately after uncrating to avoid exposure to dust, moisture, or temperature fluctuations inherent in the Angul industrial environment.</p>
<p>Clean furniture, in particular, requires careful handling to prevent scratches or dents, ensuring it remains in showroom condition for immediate use or client presentation. The positioning should align with the pre-approved floor plan to facilitate efficient workflow and minimize unnecessary movement later.</p>
<p>Finally, the swift removal of packing debris is non-negotiable for maintaining site safety and operational efficiency. All wooden crates, cardboard boxes, foam fillers, and plastic wrappings must be cleared from the delivery zone within a specified timeframe, typically no more than two hours after uncrating is complete.</p>
<p>This rapid cleanup prevents trip hazards, reduces fire risks associated with flammable packaging materials, and keeps the delivery bay accessible for incoming vehicles. Dedicated cleaning crews should be on standby to process this waste, ensuring that the Angul facility remains organized, safe, and ready for the next logistical operation without interruption or delay.</p>
